<title>UK: CE Electric rejects N.Electric defence.</title>
<headline>CE Electric rejects N.Electric defence.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. energy group CE Electric said it still believed its 630 pence per share bid for Northern Electric was full and fair despite the regional electricity company's (Rec) assertion it was too low.</p>
<p>&quot;There is nothing in Northern Electric's defence document which changes our view,&quot; the company, which is 70 percent owned by CalEnergy of the U.S., said in a statement.</p>
</text>
